item.description:
The NW 3rd Avenue Drainage Improvements Project consists of the replacement and enhancement of the City's existing stormwater drainage system along NW 3rd Avenue between NW 23rd Street and NW 20th Street, including portions of NW 21st Court and the existing outfall to the South Fork of the Middle River. The project is designed to improve the collection, conveyance, treatment, and storage of stormwater runoff to reduce roadway flooding and enhance the resiliency of the surrounding neighborhood.
Major components of the project include:
Removal and replacement of the existing stormwater drainage system;
Installation of new 24-inch, 30-inch, and 36-inch storm drainage piping;
Construction of a 30-inch perforated pipe exfiltration trench to provide stormwater storage and groundwater recharge;
